From 095aec79c0720a13ad3674277d33c8d104ec2152 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:16:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the change of mode from TMDS to HDMI FRL on
 nvidia-drm with the output off first, the menus over TMDS where its flips do
 not come back, and the logs on disk at a stall

An RTX 4080 SUPER hangs about once in ten at the change of
mode from the TMDS mode of a video back to 3840x2160 at 120 Hz over HDMI
FRL (3 of 31 with 1.0, 1 of 7 with the first builds of 1.1): the link trains and
the display says it has it, the raster of the head stands at line 0,
NVIDIA's driver goes on without the update ("Lost display notification"),
no flip comes, the next changes of mode are refused (-22), and the PC is
switched off. NVKMS shuts the head down in an update of its own before
such a mode set, and trains the link before the update of the new mode,
all in one call; what does not start is the head, in the part of the
driver that NVIDIA keeps closed. Training the link again
(nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9072) did not bring it back.

- Prevent (FRL_MODE_CHANGE::OffFirst()): such a change of mode goes out
  in two commits, the output off (CRTC ACTIVE 0) and then the new mode,
  so that NVKMS finishes the mode set that turns the head off before it
  sets the head up over FRL from an output that is off. Only where
  nvidia-drm says that the output goes over TMDS (NV_OUTPUT_LINK) and the
  new mode is one that TMDS does not carry; a refusal of the first commit
  leaves the change in one commit, as before. Whether it avoids the hang
  is measured on that card.
- Recover (FRL_MODE_CHANGE::Fallback()): where the flips do not come back
  within 60 s of a change of mode to FRL (the second stall in a row,
  CFlipStallRecovery), the menus go to the TMDS mode of the same size
  with the highest refresh rate (3840x2160 at 60 Hz), with a WARNING in
  kodi.log and a short notice, once in each failure and at most three
  times while Kodi runs. The resolution chosen in Settings stays: the
  next video and the next start go back to it. Otherwise the output is
  turned off and on again as before.
- Log: at each stall that kodi.log says, at most every 5 s, kodi.log is
  synced to disk and the journal too (journalctl --sync), off the thread
  that draws: a kodi.log once ended in zeroes 22 s before the
  end of the journal.

New strings: core 62300, Estuary 54305 (its translation), in English and
in Spanish of Spain, Argentina and Mexico.

The host test (tools/regress/kodi-host/output/presfix/
frl_mode_change_test.cpp of LibreELEC Hades) checks the three decisions on
the modes of the LG C5 and fails on each of 9 mutations of them. Not run
on a GPU.
